// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Doctor_Arvin 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Doctor Arvin 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P2206196266" "Doctor Arvin"
// ProfessionString :
"P381244892" "Physician and Genetics Researcher at Cole Memorial Hospital"
// DescriptionString :
"P1452326497" "Doctor Arvin is a well known physician within Nova Praetoria. Despite his older age, he has kept up with all of the up and coming doctors in his field. Some of his co-workers whisper that he has been working on secret experiments in his spare time, though none know what exactly he is up to.<br><br>Doctor Arvin is also known to be somewhat of a historian in his spare time, keeping an impressive collection of historical books within his home."
// InteractionRequiresText :
"P2493168063" "<color orange>You reach Dr. Arvin's voicemail when you try to call him.</color><br><br>Hello, you have reached the phone of Dr. Arvin. If you have a medical emergency, please head to Cole Memorial Hospital. If you require anything else, please leave a message."
// LocationString :
// HelloString :
"P690283936" "Make sure you have a healthy breakfast, the most important meal of the day. And none of this second-breakfast nonsense from you, either. Doctor's orders."
// IDontKnowYouString :
"P252210758" "I'm sorry, but I don't take walk-up appointments. Even though I am a physician, you'll still need to book an appointment with my receptionist. If we start breaking even the smallest rules, where would we be as a society?"
// WrongUniverseString :
"P3839145794" "You don't appear to be in need of any medical services, besides, I don't treat members of Powers Division. You should talk to Doctor Steffard, he's the expert on super human medicine."
// NoTasksRemainingString :
"P2429283815" "We've done a good job at weakening the grasp of a petty tyrant. However, as history shows us, only time will tell when we true patriots are needed again."
// PlayerBusyString :
"P2545739063" "Your dedication to eradicating the oppressors of Praetoria City is exemplary. However, you'll need to take care of your other tasks before I can ask you for further assistance."
// ComeBackLaterString :
"P4268257830" "As much as our cause can use the help, I can not in good conscience ask you to put yourself in an exceptionally dangerous situation. Perhaps if you were Security Level {Level} I would feel better about it."
// RelationshipChangeString_ToFriend :
// FailsafeLevelString :
// IntroString :
"P3559936842" "<color BurlyWood>Doctor Arvin is a very smart man, too smart, smells nice, but nice smells linger. Going to get himself into trouble one day, very big trouble. Sticks his nose where it doesn't belong, can't smell trouble like I can - can't see trouble like I can either."
// IntroAcceptString :
"P4004936930" "Speak with Dr. Arvin"
// IntroSendoffString :
"P3253268284" "<color BurlyWood>Good luck with Arvin. Try not to be around if he gets his nose chomped off by a chomper."
// IntroduceOneContact :
"P4238248219" "<color BurlyWood>Doctor Arvin, let's get this over with, the point of you meeting him. Nice man, smells nice."
// IntroduceTwoContacts :

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - DialogTree 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page HelloPage Text :
"P2072249471" "{HeroName}, good to meet you. My name is <color yellow>James Arvin.</color> As you may have guessed from my attire, I am a doctor of some repute here in Nova Praetoria.<br><br>I would love to have a casual conversation with you, but I'm afraid there is business to attend to.<br><br>You are aware of the <color red>Destroyers</color>, yes? They are a symptom of a disease spreading within Praetoria, one that I would see cured. Have you heard of it? <color yellow>Fixadine</color>? It eats away at those who cling to it, turning them into monsters. I, however, would see these monsters freed from their chains."
// Answer Text :
"P1275603798" "You have a plan to go about this?"
// Page Option1A Text :
"P727886836" "That I do. Many have tried to cure those addicted to Fixadine with little success. The main problem, you see, is that their bodies <i>require</i> Fixadine to survive - once they've become addicted, of course. It isn't a simple matter of willpower to get over the addiction. Without Fixadine, the bodily functions of those who are addicted will slowly shut down one by one, until they eventually die.<br><br>I, however, have come up with a method that will allow their bodies to sustain themselves without Fixadine. It is a long process, however, and must be done on a case by case basis.<br><br>My research was proceeding along nicely until my patient, who I have dubbed <color yellow>Subject Zero</color>, escaped from my care. This is where I need your assistance, {HeroName}."
// Answer Text :
"P1636484806" "Find Subject Zero, sounds easy enough. How did he escape?"
// Answer Text :
"P233813565" "Why not ask the PPD for help?"
// Page GoToD Text :
"P4138763470" "It was my fault, really. He was craving Fixadine for far too long. I was hoping I could create the cure before Subject Zero went into withdrawals... but time was not on my side. He easily broke out of my laboratory and is now somewhere within the city, looking for more of the drug."
// Answer Text :
"P1963656402" "Alright, do you have any idea where Subject Zero might be?"
// Page PPDHelp Text :
"P2643826985" "The PPD... don't exactly know what I'm doing. They too, are another symptom of a disease spreading in Praetoria, one that does not have to do with Fixadine.<br><br>I must keep my work a secret from them, for now. Once the cure is created, I can come forward with what I know and what I've done. There may be anger at my... activities, but my cure will easily make up for that."
// Answer Text :
"P4041578405" "How did Subject Zero get away?"
// Page GoToF Text :
"P3006519290" "I have some leads. Shall we get started?"
// Answer Text :
"P533866533" "Yes, let's figure this out."
// Answer Text :
"P3075141561" "Give me a moment."
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


